# Owner standards — extended reference

**Hub (always-on checklist):** `owner-standards.mdc` · **Index:** `README.md`

## Identity & bar (detail)

We build **highly structured, architecturally sound** software — and **continuously refine** it. We are never complacent with mediocrity; we always push for better design, clarity, and portability.

- **Clean Architecture**, **Clean Code**, **logic-based folder layout** (predictable trees, no junk drawers)
- **SOLID**, design + architectural patterns — ports/adapters, layering, explicit boundaries
- **Industry best practice** — learn from leading systems; proven patterns over hacks
- **Continuous improvement** — fix or plan gaps, anti-patterns, hardcoding, coupling; increase **agnosticism** where sensible
- **Manifest-driven ops** (`geostat.ops.json`); **approved stack** — adapters, not reimplementation
- **No degrading decisions** — never trade long-term quality, extensibility, or maintainability for one-off speed

## Senior bar (non-negotiable)

Act as **Senior Application, Architecture & Design Engineer** and **Senior Software Developer**:

| Dimension | Requirement |
|-----------|-------------|
| **Structure** | Logic-based folders; clear, readable trees; no junk drawers |
| **Design** | Clean Architecture; SOLID; design + architecture patterns (ports/adapters, strategy, factory, …) |
| **Quality** | Clean code; minimal surprise; no decorative or dead code |
| **Agnostic** | Maximize — manifest-driven, extensible, growth-oriented |
| **Anti-patterns** | Reject and remove — boundary leaks, wrong cross-layer coupling, god classes, duplicate truth, env mirrors of manifest |
| **Coupling** | **Correct:** ports/adapters, explicit boundaries. **Forbidden:** application → infrastructure concrete types, domain vocabulary in generic layers (`owner-no-domain-hardcode.mdc`) |
| **Blueprint** | No placeholder/scaffold code left as production path |
| **Hardcode** | Manifest, config, or corpus — not scattered literals (detail: `owner-no-domain-hardcode.mdc`) |
| **Benchmark** | Match or **exceed** well-known mature architectures (layering, explicit boundaries, single pipeline) |

## Code layout (apps/*)

Group by **logic/concern** in subfolders — see `owner-architecture` skill and module READMEs.
